#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:4
msgid ""
"Route this delivery request to the `feature-delivery-lead` agent for "
"execution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:6
msgid ""
"Be the `feature-delivery-lead` agent. Load the `context-injection` skill "
"before starting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:8
msgid ""
"**Before starting work**, emit a `hero next ask` capturing what the user "
"asked for. This preserves session intent across compaction — see the "
"`next-handoff-emit` skill for the full pattern (ask / suggest / "
"reflection)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:12
msgid "Delivery modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:14
msgid ""
"Parse the mode from the user's invocation. If no mode is specified, "
"default to **supervised**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md
msgid "Flag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md
msgid "Behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md
msgid "`--supervised` (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md
msgid ""
"Pause at handoffs, surface decisions, ask before destructive actions. "
"Current behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md
msgid "`--autopilot`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md
msgid ""
"Run to completion without intermediate confirmations. Stop only on test "
"failure, drift warning, boundary violation, or any non-`DONE` Completion "
"Ledger item (PARTIAL, SKIPPED, BLOCKED)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md
msgid "`--dry-run`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md
msgid ""
"Run analysis and planning. Produce a delivery plan (file list, agent "
"assignments, estimated changes) but write NO code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:23
msgid "Autopilot mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:25
msgid ""
"Suppress confirmation prompts during the delivery loop. Check `hero "
"drift` after implementation, run tests if a runner is configured, "
"validate the engineer's **Completion Ledger** against the spec, and:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:28
msgid ""
"**PARTIAL rows:** loop back to the engineer with instructions to finish "
"them. Do not halt. Only escalate if a second pass returns PARTIAL on the "
"same row with a specific written obstacle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:31
msgid "**SKIPPED / BLOCKED rows:** halt and surface — these need user judgment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:32
msgid "**Test failure / drift warning / boundary violation:** halt and surface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:34
msgid ""
"If `--halt-on` is provided (comma-separated: `drift`, `test`, `boundary`,"
" `lint`, `ledger`), only halt on those specific conditions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:37
msgid ""
"Persistence rule (`agent-reliability` — \"Persistence on continuous "
"tasks\") applies: do not yield between phases unless a true blocker "
"fires. PARTIAL is NOT a blocker — finish the work. SKIPPED and BLOCKED "
"ARE blockers — halt and surface. \"This is taking a while\" is NOT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:42
msgid "Dry-run mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:44
msgid "Produce a plan at `.hero/planning/features/<slug>/plan.md`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:46
msgid ""
"# Delivery plan — <slug>\n"
"Generated: <timestamp>\n"
"Mode: dry-run\n"
"\n"
"## Tasks (sequenced)\n"
"1. [specialist] description → target-file (~N lines)\n"
"2. ...\n"
"\n"
"## Risks\n"
"- boundary checks, drift baseline, potential conflicts\n"
"\n"
"## Estimated complexity\n"
"~N lines, N specialist handoffs, ~N minutes wall time\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:62
msgid "Do NOT write any source files. The plan file is the only output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:64
msgid "Batch mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:66
msgid ""
"If the user asks to fix/deliver multiple specs (e.g. \"fix the researched"
" bugs\", \"deliver the 5 planned features\"):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:68
msgid ""
"Run `hero search --list --type bug --status planning` (or the appropriate"
" type/status) to find candidate specs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:69
msgid ""
"Filter to specs that have a `## Suggested Fix Approach` or `## Changes` "
"section — these are the ones with a plan ready to execute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:70
msgid ""
"Present the list to the user for confirmation: \"Found N specs ready to "
"deliver: [list]. Proceeding with all of them sequentially.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:71
msgid "**Work through them sequentially, one at a time.** Each fix:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:72
msgid "Read the spec and its fix plan"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:73
msgid "Implement the fix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:74
msgid "Run tests / build to verify"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:75
msgid ""
"Require a **Completion Ledger** from the engineer covering every "
"acceptance criterion and Changes item (see `engineer.md` — \"Closing "
"output\"). Validate it against the spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:76
msgid "Commit with a message referencing the spec slug and tracker ID"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:77
msgid ""
"Only set `status: completed` if the ledger is fully `DONE`. PARTIAL rows "
"are sent back to the engineer to finish (see \"Validate the Completion "
"Ledger\" above); SKIPPED / BLOCKED rows halt and surface — do not flip "
"status without sign-off. `hero spec verify` or the async runner will "
"auto-archive completed specs to specs/."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:78
msgid "Post results to tracker if configured"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:79
msgid "**One commit per fix** — each fix is atomic and independently revertable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:80
msgid ""
"If a fix fails tests or creates problems, skip it, note the issue in the "
"spec, and move to the next one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:81
msgid "At the end, summarize: N fixed, N skipped (with reasons)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:83
msgid ""
"**Do not parallelize fixes** — they may touch overlapping code and create"
" conflicts. Sequential delivery ensures each fix builds on a clean, "
"tested codebase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:85
msgid "Queue mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:87
msgid ""
"When the user says \"deliver these while I'm away\", \"queue these up\", "
"or provides a list of slugs with `--autopilot`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:90
msgid "Validate all specs are ready (have Changes section, pass quality gate)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:91
msgid "Sort by dependency order using `hero_sequence`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:92
msgid ""
"Show the queue and get one confirmation: \"Will deliver N specs in order:"
" [list]. Mode: autopilot. I'll halt on test failures, boundary "
"violations, or non-`DONE` Completion Ledger items.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:95
msgid "Execute sequentially using the autopilot flow for each"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:96
msgid ""
"Between each spec: run `hero drift`, run tests, validate the Completion "
"Ledger, commit atomically"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:98
msgid ""
"If a spec returns PARTIAL rows: loop the engineer to finish them before "
"moving on — do not move to the next spec with PARTIAL rows unhandled. If "
"a spec returns SKIPPED / BLOCKED rows or a test/drift failure: log the "
"failure, skip the spec (do NOT flip to `completed`), continue with the "
"next."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:103
msgid ""
"At the end: summary of delivered (fully `DONE`), halted (with SKIPPED / "
"BLOCKED rows for user judgment), and failed (with reasons). PARTIAL "
"should not appear in the final summary — it should have been resolved in "
"step 6."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:108
msgid "Single spec mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:110
msgid ""
"For a single spec delivery, follow the standard pre-flight and delivery "
"workflow as the `feature-delivery-lead` agent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:112
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Pre-flight — check for mockups.** Before delegating to the engineer, "
"check whether `.hero/mocks/{slug}/` exists for the spec being delivered. "
"If it does, list the file paths inside it in the kickoff context handed "
"to the engineer (e.g. \"Mockups available for this spec: "
"`.hero/mocks/{slug}/index.html` — read if a visual reference helps.\"). "
"Don't render or quote the HTML; let the engineer open it if useful. The "
"same check applies in batch and queue modes — surface mockup paths in the"
" kickoff for each spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:114
msgid "At the end of the delivery loop:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:116
msgid ""
"**Check for drift** — verify the implementation matches the spec. Address"
" any divergence before moving on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:118
msgid ""
"**Verify and expand test coverage** — confirm every acceptance criterion "
"has a corresponding test. When fixing a bug, add a regression test that "
"reproduces the original failure. Look at the code you touched and the "
"code around it — if adjacent functions or modules lack test coverage, add"
" tests for them too. Match the project's existing test patterns and "
"framework. The goal is to leave coverage better than you found it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:124
msgid ""
"**Run the test suite** — make sure everything passes, including the tests"
" you just wrote and any existing tests for the affected area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:126
msgid ""
"**Link tests to criteria** — connect each new test back to the acceptance"
" criterion it verifies so regressions are traceable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:128
msgid ""
"**Validate the Completion Ledger** — the engineer's closing artifact (see"
" `engineer.md` — \"Closing output\") enumerates every acceptance "
"criterion and every `## Changes` item with a `DONE` / `PARTIAL` / "
"`SKIPPED` / `BLOCKED` status. Before flipping spec status:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:132
msgid "Confirm every acceptance criterion and every Changes item has a row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:133
msgid ""
"Cross-check each `DONE` against actual code and test evidence on disk. "
"Challenge performative `DONE` marks; downgrade rows that lack evidence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:135
msgid ""
"For user-visible behavior, confirm the Exercise-the-feature check is "
"populated — unit tests alone are not sufficient evidence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:137
msgid ""
"**PARTIAL is not an acceptable end state — finish the work.** PARTIAL "
"means the engineer ran out of time, energy, or attention, not that the "
"work is intrinsically un-doable. Do NOT ask the user \"ship as-is or "
"chase these down?\" — the standing answer is *chase them down*. Send the "
"ledger back to the engineer with the PARTIAL rows and explicit "
"instructions to complete them, then re-validate. Only after a second pass"
" *still* returns PARTIAL on the same row — with a written reason that "
"names a specific obstacle (not \"minor polish,\" not \"low value\") — may"
" you surface it to the user. The bar: would a careful engineer reading "
"this spec next week consider the work finished? If no, keep working."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:148
msgid ""
"**SKIPPED and BLOCKED** are legitimate human-judgment escalations. "
"SKIPPED needs the user's call on scope; BLOCKED names a real external "
"obstacle. Surface these with the specific row, the engineer's stated "
"reason, and a concrete recommendation — not an open-ended question."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:152
msgid ""
"Do NOT flip to `completed` while any row remains non-`DONE`. In autopilot"
" mode, PARTIAL re-enters the engineer loop automatically; SKIPPED / "
"BLOCKED halt the run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:155
msgid ""
"**Cold audit pass** — once the ledger is fully `DONE` (or non-`DONE` rows"
" have explicit user sign-off), spawn a **fresh** subagent to audit the "
"delivery before you flip status. This is the second set of eyes the lead "
"cannot be, because the lead watched the work happen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:160
msgid ""
"Invoke a general-purpose subagent with the `delivery-audit` skill loaded."
" Hand it ONLY artifacts on disk — no commentary, no framing, no \"this "
"looks good to me\":"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:163
msgid "Spec path (absolute)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:164
msgid "Diff command (`git diff <base>...HEAD` or equivalent)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:165
msgid "The engineer's Completion Ledger, verbatim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:166
msgid "Test evidence (paths to test output, exercise notes)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:168
msgid "The audit writes a durable report file to disk and returns three blocks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:170
msgid ""
"`<AUDIT_VERDICT>` — verdict (SHIP/HOLD), surface (noteworthy/clean), "
"confidence, report_path"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:172
msgid ""
"`<AUDIT_HEADLINE>` — **always populated**, the delivery receipt: AC "
"count, audit verdict, report path, then a **New files** table, a "
"**Modified files** table (each with a one-line description of what each "
"file does or what changed), and a **Tests** summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:176
msgid ""
"`<AUDIT_HIGHLIGHTS>` — populated when surface=noteworthy or verdict=HOLD;"
" 1–5 bullets naming specific concerns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:179
msgid "Route based on the verdict:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:181
msgid ""
"**HOLD** → do NOT flip to `completed`. Read the highlights and the report"
" file, route the specific concerns back to the engineer to address, re-"
"validate the ledger, re-run the audit. **Bounded retry:** if the same row"
" returns HOLD after 2 engineer passes, stop looping and escalate to the "
"user with the auditor's concerns and a concrete recommendation. Do not "
"grind indefinitely — a row that resists two focused passes usually needs "
"human judgment (the spec was wrong, the approach was wrong, or a "
"dependency is missing). Surface that, don't paper over it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:190
msgid ""
"**SHIP + noteworthy** → quote the full `<AUDIT_HEADLINE>` (file tables "
"and all) AND the `<AUDIT_HIGHLIGHTS>` bullets in your final response. "
"Link to the full report at `report_path`. Proceed to step 7."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:194
msgid ""
"**SHIP + clean** → quote the full `<AUDIT_HEADLINE>` (file tables and "
"all) in your final response. The receipt is earned signal on every "
"delivery — do NOT collapse it to a one-liner. What you skip on a clean "
"SHIP is the highlights block (because there's nothing to flag), not the "
"inventory. Proceed to step 7."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:200
msgid "**What's always shown vs. conditional:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:201
msgid ""
"**Always:** the full headline — what landed, file-by-file, plus test "
"summary. This is the durable delivery receipt the user reads on every "
"delivery; it's the only scannable record of what changed without diving "
"into the diff."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:205
msgid ""
"**Conditional (only when noteworthy or HOLD):** highlights — downgrades, "
"soft skips, concerns the auditor wants the user's eyes on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:208
msgid ""
"**Always written to disk, linked from chat:** the full report file for "
"when the user wants depth (evidence, line numbers, full reasoning)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:212
msgid ""
"The signal-preservation rule is: make **highlights** conditional, not the"
" inventory. A clean SHIP still gets the full file table — that's the "
"point of running the audit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:216
msgid ""
"Do not skip this step in supervised mode. The cost is one subagent call; "
"the value is catching performative `DONE` rows AND producing a durable "
"delivery record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:219
msgid ""
"**Refresh the kickoff** — when status flips (planning → delivering, "
"delivering → completed) or after meaningful chunks land, rewrite the "
"spec's `## Kickoff` section so \"Pick up at:\" reflects *now*, not \"two "
"commits ago.\" Follow the `kickoff-prompt` skill. After mutating the "
"spec, run `hero index --if-stale -q` so the new state surfaces in `hero "
"search` / `hero list` / `hero_*` MCP tools immediately. The pre-commit "
"hook will refresh `.hero/QUEUE.md` automatically; if you're not "
"committing right away, run `hero queue write -q` to refresh the snapshot "
"manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:228
msgid ""
"**Suggest what's next** — your final response to the user must end with a"
" concrete \"Next up\" suggestion. Not a list of options to choose from, "
"not \"let me know what you want to do\" — a single recommended next move,"
" named specifically. Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:233
msgid ""
"\"Next up: deliver `<dep-slug>` — it's the only remaining blocker on "
"`<parent-slug>`.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:235
msgid ""
"\"Next up: open the PR for this branch (`gh pr create`) and request "
"review from the team.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:237
msgid ""
"\"Next up: run `/diagnose <bug-slug>` — it's the highest-severity bug in "
"the queue and touches code adjacent to what we just changed.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:239
msgid ""
"\"Next up: take a break — the active spec list is empty and the queue is "
"healthy.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:242
msgid ""
"Use `hero_kickoff` or `hero_pulse` to inform the suggestion if you're "
"uncertain. Always emit the suggestion via the `next-handoff-emit` pattern"
" so it lands in `.hero/NEXT.md` and the per-user handoff file — that way "
"the next session resumes with the same recommendation visible from the "
"first prompt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:248
msgid ""
"When delivery is complete and the Completion Ledger is fully `DONE` (or "
"non-`DONE` rows have explicit user sign-off), set the spec's `status: "
"completed` in the frontmatter and run `hero spec verify <slug>` — verify "
"auto-archives a completed spec to `.hero/specs/<slug>/`, so you don't "
"need a separate `hero spec complete` step. The async runner does the same"
" auto-archive at the tail of every successful agent delivery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:255
msgid ""
"Do not hand-write `completed_at:` when you flip the status — `hero spec "
"verify` stamps the canonical timestamp automatically (RFC 3339 UTC) so "
"downstream consumers like the Sprint Dashboard read an authoritative "
"value. Hand-writing the field is harmless (idempotent) but unnecessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:260
msgid ""
"The Completion Ledger replaces the older \"implementation summary\" "
"pattern. Soft prose summaries that gloss skipped or partial work are "
"explicitly out — the ledger is the artifact of record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:264
msgid "Spec-to-PR linking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:266
msgid ""
"After completing delivery, if the work was committed on a branch with an "
"open PR (check with `gh pr view` or equivalent), annotate the PR:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:269
msgid ""
"Add a comment linking back to the spec: \"Delivered from Hero spec: "
"`<slug>` — <title>\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:270
msgid "If the spec has a `tracker_id`, mention it in the PR description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:271
msgid ""
"If a tracker is configured, use `hero_claim` to update the tracker issue "
"with the PR link"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:274
msgid "This closes the spec→code→PR chain so reviewers can trace requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/deliver.md:276
msgid "Spec or work item: $ARGUMENTS"
msgstr ""

